WEBVTT
Kind: subtitles
Language: en

NOTE
English subtitles for "The UAE Through History" (IRTH). Translated from the on-screen Arabic text.

1
00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:25.000
The United Arab Emirates
A journey through history over a single map, from ancient times to the founding of the Union.

2
00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:29.000
6000 BC — The Stone Age
The first human communities settle on the shores of the Gulf, living by hunting and gathering food.

3
00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:33.000
3200–1300 BC — The Bronze Age
The Umm an-Nar civilisation flourishes, with circular tombs and early land and sea trade networks.

4
00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:37.000
1300–300 BC — The Iron Age
The falaj system is invented to irrigate the oases, and farming spreads across the inland areas.

5
00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:41.000
630 AD — Islam reaches the region
The tribes of the region embrace Islam, and the Islamic era begins in the history of the Emirates.

6
00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:45.000
The Islamic eras — Seafaring flourishes
Shipbuilding and pearl diving thrive, and sea trade routes flourish between the ports.

7
00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:50.000
1722 — The first rulers of Ras Al Khaimah and Sharjah
Sheikh Rahma bin Matar Al Qasimi founded the Al Qasimi family in Ras Al Khaimah in 1722, and the family ruled both emirates before Sharjah officially became an independently ruled emirate in 1921.

8
00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:55.000
1761 — The first ruler of Abu Dhabi
Sheikh Dhiyab bin Isa Al Nahyan led the Bani Yas tribe and ruled Abu Dhabi from 1761, founding the ruling Al Nahyan family.

9
00:00:55.000 --> 00:01:00.000
1768 — The first ruler of Umm Al Quwain
Sheikh Rashid bin Majid Al Mualla built the fort of Umm Al Quwain and became its ruler in 1768, founding the ruling Al Mualla family.

10
00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:05.000
1816 — The first ruler of Ajman
Sheikh Rashid bin Humaid Al Nuaimi became Ruler of Ajman in 1816, founding the ruling Al Nuaimi family.

11
00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:10.000
1833 — The first ruler of Dubai
Sheikh Maktoum bin Butti Al Maktoum established independent rule in Dubai in 1833, founding the ruling Al Maktoum family.

12
00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:15.000
1879 — The first ruler of Fujairah
Sheikh Hamad bin Abdullah Al Sharqi founded the ruling Al Sharqi family in 1879, and Fujairah was recognised as independent in 1952.

13
00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:19.500
18 February 1968 — The Argoub Al Sedirah meeting
Sheikh Zayed bin Sultan Al Nahyan and Sheikh Rashid bin Saeed Al Maktoum meet, and the path to the Union begins.

14
00:01:19.500 --> 00:01:25.000
2 December 1971 — The founding of the United Arab Emirates
Six emirates unite: Abu Dhabi, Dubai, Sharjah, Ajman, Umm Al Quwain and Fujairah.

15
00:01:25.000 --> 00:01:29.500
10 February 1972 — The Union of the seven emirates is complete
Ras Al Khaimah joins the Union, completing the seven emirates.

16
00:01:29.500 --> 00:01:33.500
A glimpse of each emirate
After the founding of the Union, here is a brief history of each of the seven emirates.

17
00:01:33.500 --> 00:01:37.500
Emirate 1 of 7 — Abu Dhabi
Founded by the Bani Yas tribe and ruled by the Al Nahyan family, it is home to ancient sites such as Hili in Al Ain, and became the federal capital after its economy flourished following the discovery of oil.

18
00:01:37.500 --> 00:01:43.500
Emirate 2 of 7 — Dubai
It thrived as a trading port on Dubai Creek, ruled by the Al Maktoum family since the 19th century, and was known for pearl diving and sea trade before later becoming a global business hub.

19
00:01:43.500 --> 00:01:49.500
Emirate 3 of 7 — Sharjah
Ruled by the Al Qasimi family, it is unique in overlooking both the Arabian Gulf and the Gulf of Oman, and was historically known for its naval strength and cultural standing.

20
00:01:49.500 --> 00:01:55.000
Emirate 4 of 7 — Ajman
The smallest emirate by area, ruled by the Al Nuaimi family; its people were historically known for building wooden ships and for fishing.

21
00:01:55.000 --> 00:01:59.500
Emirate 5 of 7 — Umm Al Quwain
Ruled by the Al Mualla family, its people relied on pearling and fishing, and its land holds the ed-Dur archaeological site, which dates back to before Islam.

22
00:01:59.500 --> 00:02:05.000
Emirate 6 of 7 — Ras Al Khaimah
It grew around the historic port of Julfar, once one of the most important ports in the Gulf; ruled by the Al Qasimi family, it was the last emirate to join the Union, in 1972.

23
00:02:05.000 --> 00:02:10.500
Emirate 7 of 7 — Fujairah
The only emirate lying entirely on the coast of the Gulf of Oman, ruled by the Al Sharqi family, which gained British recognition of it as an independent emirate in 1952.

24
00:02:11.000 --> 00:02:21.000
The United Arab Emirates
Seven emirates • One history • One Union
